# Source manifest — reproducible-by-reference (Invariant 3).
# Re-clone at build time; the working tree under sources/datamodel-code-generator/
# is gitignored.
#
# R6: the named source of truth for generated models. R10 PASS, last commit
# 2026-08-06. Note the dotfiles session found it silently drops
# `unevaluatedProperties: false` for msgspec output — refuting or confirming that
# is R11 work and needs this source in the graph.
#
# Ray, 2026-08-19: a CRITICAL/currency dependency this repo must SYNC with.
# `[tool.datamodel-code-generator]` in `currency.toml` now checks this pin.
#
# ⚠️ THIS PIN WAS `ref = main` UNTIL 2026-08-19 — a BRANCH HEAD, which every
# other manifest here explicitly forbids ("Pin the RELEASE TAG, never a branch
# head — a branch drifts ahead of the release"). A branch pin makes the corpus
# describe unreleased code and makes the clone non-reproducible: the same
# manifest resolves to different bytes on different days. Fixed to the release
# tag matching the version we declare.
#
# ⚠️ INVARIANT: this pin MUST track the version we actually declare.
#   version source: pyproject.toml `[dependency-groups] codegen` EXACT pin
#                   `datamodel-code-generator==0.75.1`, confirmed against
#                   `datamodel-codegen --version`.
#   pinned here:    0.76.0
#
#   This block said 0.74.0 until 2026-08-28 while `ref` beside it already read
#   0.75.1 — the machine-read values were correct and only the prose restating
#   them had gone stale. Which is the argument for not restating a pin in prose
#   at all; it is kept because the INVARIANT above needs something to name.
#
# ⚠️ IT IS INVOKED — three generators depend on it, and this file nearly shipped
# claiming the opposite. The claim was "DECLARED BUT NOT YET INVOKED", sourced to
# `docs/directives-2026-08-08.md`'s `git log -S datamodel --all` -> 0 hits: an
# INHERITED NUMBER, true on 2026-08-08 and false eleven days later. Ingesting the
# source matters MORE for that, not less — the graph is being asked "what does
# this emit?" about code we already ship.
#
# ⚠️ SUPERSEDED 2026-08-28 (#569): the three wrapper scripts below — and the
# fourth, research-record, added after this block was written — are DELETED.
# Nothing in this repo hand-writes the plumbing that invokes the generator any
# more: `[tool.datamodel-codegen.jobs.*]` in pyproject.toml declares four jobs,
# and `mise run kb-codegen` / `kb-codegen-check` run the native
# `--all-jobs` / `--all-jobs --check`. The mapping is kept as the historical
# record of what shipped at the 2026-08-19 investigation, NOT as current layout.
#
#   schemas/generate_fetch_receipt.py  -> python/src/kb_setup/generated/fetch_receipt.py
#   schemas/generate_source_groups.py  -> python/src/kb_setup/generated/source_groups.py
#   schemas/generate_session_select.py -> python/src/kb_setup/generated/session_select.py
#
# It is still INVOKED, which is what that heading is about — by a mise task now
# rather than by a script. This second copy of the mapping went un-updated when
# `currency.toml`'s copy got its own superseded note, and a cold review caught
# it: a revision restated in two places gets amended in one.
#
# 0.73.0's breaking changes cost this repo nothing, but by MEASUREMENT rather
# than by absence: all three regenerated byte-identically at 0.74.0. That
# sentence is a past measurement and stays in the past tense; the equivalent
# measurement at 0.75.1 is the drift gate, which runs on every `mise run test`.
#
# ⚠️ TAGS CARRY NO `v` PREFIX — the tag is `0.75.1`, not `v0.75.1`, so a
# `v<x>`-only resolver finds nothing and an apply aborts rather than mispinning.
# Same class as `[tool.codex]`'s `rust-v<version>`, opposite direction. Both
# routes agree on the commit here (lightweight tag), unlike agnix.
#
# ⚠️ AND ITS VERSION LITERAL IS LOAD-BEARING IN A TEST (#396).
# `tests/test_skillopt_contract.py` `.replace()`s the exact string
# `codegen = ["datamodel-code-generator==<version>"]` inside a copy of the REAL
# pyproject.toml. Bumping the pin without updating that literal makes the
# replace a silent no-op and the assertion fails. It also depends on the array
# being on ONE LINE: `uv add` writes it multi-line and taplo collapses it back,
# so run `mise run fmt` before `pytest`.
#
# To bump: `uv add --group codegen 'datamodel-code-generator==<version>'`,
# update both test literals, `mise run fmt`, then set ref/commit here:
#   mise ls-remote datamodel-code-generator      # Ray's directive, #395
#   gh api repos/koxudaxi/datamodel-code-generator/commits/<version> --jq .sha
# then `mise run kb-build`.
#
# kind = code: AST extraction only, no LLM, no cost.
url = https://github.com/koxudaxi/datamodel-code-generator
ref = 0.76.0
commit = 1e422243c189636b11b776f29a5b42972b0cad0e
kind = code
